          name: "Why does my watch show fewer steps than this after 30 minutes?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually because your arms were not swinging. Wrist trackers count steps mostly from arm movement, so holding the handrails or resting on a desk can make them miss many steps. Walk hands-free, or wear a phone or clip-on counter at your hip if you need the rails.",
          },
